  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1248 PM MST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nTransatory ridging builds across the region into Wednesday, leading \nto dry conditions and warming temperatures. Latest operational and \nensemble model data coming into better agreement of more eastern \nPacific energy splitting as it translates across the Intermountain \nWest Thursday and Friday. This will keep the region in moderate \nnorthwest flow into the end of the Thanksgiving Holiday weekend, \nwith chances of precipitation confined mainly to the Northern and \nCentral Mtns, and temperatures remaining at or slightly above \nseasonal levels. However, will need to continue to monitor the \npotential for surface high pressure building across the Northern \nHigh Plains to send a backdoor cold front into eastern Colorado\nlater next weekend.",
